course: dictionary
lesson: 4234
title: Words for family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Granddad is a friendly, informal word for your grandfather, the father of your mum or dad. Context tells you who is meant. In «"Batteries in the fridge!" says Granddad.», the words "says Granddad" show that Granddad is the person speaking.
explain: Context also tells you when granddad is a name. «Hi, Granddad!» uses a capital letter because Granddad is the name you call him. In «My granddad likes fishing», it is an ordinary word, so it starts with a small letter.
explain: Clue words help too. If a sentence says "my granddad" or "your granddad", you know it means one particular grandfather. To check your meaning, swap in another word such as "grandpa" or "grandfather". If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning fits.
fact: Granddad is a noun: one granddad, two granddads.
fact: Granddad means the father of your mum or dad.
fact: Granddad is friendly and informal; grandfather is more formal.
fact: Other words for granddad include Grandpa, Gramps and Pop.
fact: Use a capital letter when Granddad is a name, as in «Hi, Granddad!»
exercise: «"Batteries in the fridge!" says Granddad.» Who is speaking? | The fridge | A bus driver | A baby | *Granddad
exercise: Which sentence uses granddad as a common noun, not as a name? | *My granddad taught me to fish. | Thanks, Granddad. | Granddad, come quick! | Hi, Granddad!
exercise: What does granddad mean? | Your big brother | A friend from school | A grandmother | *The father of your mum or dad
test: What is the plural of granddad? | granddad's | *granddads | grandaddies
test: Which word is the more formal word for granddad? | Gramps | Grandpa | *Grandfather | Pop
exam: Which sentence uses Granddad as a name? | I saw a granddad at the park. | *Hi, Granddad! | The granddads walked their dogs. | My granddad likes gardening.
